---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import Base from "../layouts/base.astro";
import NormalBlock from "../components/normal_block.astro";
import Boxes from "../components/boxes.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/page_header.astro";
import Card from "../components/card.astro";
import BookButton from "../components/book_button.astro";

import { commonData } from "../components/common_data.astro";

import wardrobe1 from "../assets/images/photos/wardrobe_1.jpg";
import wardrobe2 from "../assets/images/photos/wardrobe_2.jpg";
import wardrobe3 from "../assets/images/photos/wardrobe_3.jpg";

const metadata = {
    title: "Wardrobe Edit | Personal Styling in Glasgow",
    description: "Transform your wardrobe with a personalised wardrobe edit in Glasgow. Declutter, create outfits and learn how to dress with confidence using what you already own",
    type: "website",
};
---

<Base metadata={metadata}>
    <PageHeader title="Wardrobe Edit" />
    <NormalBlock title="What if getting dressed could feel easy, enjoyable and truly like you?">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-8 items-center">
            <div>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Do you ever look into your wardrobe and feel that you have plenty of clothes,
                    yet somehow nothing to wear?</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Perhaps your style no longer reflects who you are. Maybe your body, lifestyle or 
                    taste has changed, and your wardrobe simply hasn't caught up.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Or perhaps you already have many beautiful pieces, but you are not sure how to combine
                    them, what works for you, or how to make the most of what you already own.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">If any of this sounds familiar, a <strong>Wardrobe Edit</strong> could be the fresh
                    start you need.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">This is not about telling you what you should or shouldn't wear. It is a collaborative
                    process in which we work together to create a wardrobe that feels authentic to you, works for your lifestyle
                    and makes getting dressed easier.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">My role is to give you the knowledge, guidance and confidence to make your own choices –
                    not only while we are working together, but long after our sessions have finished.</p>
            </div>
            <Image class="min-h-full md:max-h-[700px] xl:max-h-[560px] object-cover justify-self-center pb-4 md:order-first" src={wardrobe1} alt="" />
        </div>
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="A wardrobe that works for you" bgClass="bg-pic-jumpers">
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Every Wardrobe Edit is tailored to your individual needs. Depending on your goals,
            we may focus on one or both of the following:</p>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <h4>Wardrobe Editing & Decluttering</h4>
            <p>Together, we identify the pieces that no longer serve you – whether they no longer fit, no longer reflect
                your personality, or simply haven't been worn in years. Creating space allows us to see your wardrobe
                with fresh eyes and discover what is already there.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-3">
            <h4>Outfit Creation</h4>
            <p>We use your existing clothes to create practical, versatile outfits for your everyday life, work, special
                occasions or particular seasons. You may be surprised by how many possibilities are already hiding in
                your wardrobe.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">During the process, we will also create a personalised <strong>wishlist</strong> of pieces
            or accessories that could genuinely enhance your wardrobe. The aim is not to encourage unnecessary shopping,
            but to help you make more intentional choices in the future.</p>
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="How does it work?">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-8 items-center">
            <div>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">The Wardrobe Edit is designed as a three-step journey.</p>
                <div class="mb-3">
                    <h4>1. Discovery Consultation – approximately 45 minutes</h4>
                    <p>We begin with an online or in-person consultation to get to know each other and understand what you would
                        like to change. We will talk about your lifestyle, current wardrobe, personal style, challenges and goals.
                        You will also receive a questionnaire to complete, helping me build a more detailed picture of your needs.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-3">
                    <h4>2. Style & Body Shape Consultation – approximately 45 minutes</h4>
                    <p>In our second session, we look more closely at your body shape, lifestyle and style preferences. We will
                        review your questionnaire together and explore what currently works for you – and what doesn't. This session
                        can take place in person or online. We will then plan your Wardrobe Edit and agree on the date for our
                        practical session.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="mb-3">
                    <h4>3. The Wardrobe Edit – approximately 3 hours</h4>
                    <p>This is where everything comes together. In your own home, we will go through your wardrobe, organise your
                        clothes and create new combinations from the pieces you already own. I will show you how to use your wardrobe
                        more intentionally and how to choose clothes that work with your body shape, lifestyle and personality.
                        We will also create your personal wishlist, identifying any key pieces or accessories that would fill genuine
                        gaps in your wardrobe. The goal is simple: to open your wardrobe in the morning and feel inspired rather than
                        overwhelmed.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <Image class="min-h-full md:max-h-[700px] xl:max-h-[560px] object-cover justify-self-center pb-4" src={wardrobe2} alt="" />
        </div>
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="What you will take away" bgClass="bg-pic-scarves">
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">A Wardrobe Edit is not simply about having a tidier wardrobe. You will gain:</p>
    <Boxes items={[
        { title: 'A better understanding of your body shape', text: 'So you can recognise why certain cuts and silhouettes work particularly well for you.'},
        { title: 'Practical styling knowledge', text: 'You will learn how to combine your existing clothes and create outfits with confidence.'},
        { title: 'A more intentional wardrobe', text: 'Instead of constantly looking for something new, you will learn to make better use of what you already have.'},
        { title: 'Greater confidence', text: 'The aim is for your clothes to support how you want to feel – comfortable, confident and authentically yourself.'},
        { title: 'A personalised wardrobe wishlist', text: 'A clear guide to what is genuinely missing, helping you shop with more purpose in the future.'},
    ]}/>
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="This is a journey, not a quick makeover">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-8 items-center">
            <div>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Real change takes time.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">My approach is not about giving you a list of rules or creating a completely different version
                    of you overnight. It is about helping you understand yourself better and giving you practical tools that you can
                    continue using independently.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">You may have some unexpected discoveries and plenty of "aha" moments along the way – but most
                    importantly, I want you to enjoy the process.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Your wardrobe should never ask you to become someone you are not.</p>
                <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">It should help you express who you already are.</p>
            </div>
            <Image class="min-h-full md:max-h-[700px] xl:max-h-[560px] object-cover justify-self-center pb-4 md:order-first" src={wardrobe3} alt="" />
        </div>
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="Investment" bgClass="bg-pic-street">
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6"><strong>Wardrobe Edit: {commonData.prices.wardrobeEdit}</strong></p>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">The service includes:</p>
        <ul class="list-image-checkmark-sm md:list-image-checkmark-md list-outside relative left-4 md:left-5 mb-3 md:mb-6">
            <li>a 45-minute discovery consultation</li>
            <li>a 45-minute style and body shape consultation</li>
            <li>a 3-hour practical Wardrobe Edit in your home</li>
            <li>personalised styling guidance</li>
            <li>outfit creation using your existing wardrobe</li>
            <li>a personalised wardrobe wishlist</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">A <strong>50% deposit</strong> is required to secure your Wardrobe Edit appointment.</p>
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="A little extra for your colour journey">
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Have you not yet experienced a Colour Analysis with me?</p>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">After completing your Wardrobe Edit, you can receive <strong>20% off a Colour Analysis</strong>,
            provided you book it within six months.</p>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Colour is an important part of creating a wardrobe that truly works for you. Once you understand
            which colours enhance your natural appearance, we can bring that knowledge into your wardrobe and make your outfit
            choices even more effortless.</p>
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="Ready to open your wardrobe with fresh eyes?" bgClass="bg-pic-shop">
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Book your <strong>free 15-minute consultation</strong> and let's talk about what you would like to change,
            what is currently not working for you, and how I can help.</p>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6">Your wardrobe doesn't need to be bigger. It simply needs to work better for you.</p>
        <p class="mb-3 md:mb-6 italic">Initial consultations can be online or in person. The 3-hour Wardrobe Edit takes place in your home.</p>
        <BookButton />
    </NormalBlock>
    <NormalBlock title="Testimonials" bgClass="">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-[80%]">
            <Card author="Pippa">
                I had a fantastic wardrobe edit session with Aniko. My goal for the session was to learn to mix and match existing pieces, and combine
                different aspects of my style into new outfits. We definitely achieved this!  She used her expertise from a previous colour analysis,
                combined with a body shape analysis, to look at my wardrobe with fresh eyes. With my personal style in mind, she created bold new
                combinations I never would've thought of.<br/><br/>

                She encouraged me not to hide my figure in oversized clothes. One of her best styling tips was tucking in t-shirts to complement my
                hourglass shape, a simple trick that has made a big difference.<br/><br/>

                As a mum, it was such a luxury to take some time to focus on myself and my style. Aniko put me at ease straight away and really focused
                on my own style and goals. I highly recommend Aniko for anyone looking to refresh their wardrobe and style with expert guidance.
            </Card>
            <Card author="Lujzi">
                She was very good at listening to my needs and my opinions throughout the consultation. She helped me piece things together I never
                thought I’d be able to, and was very supportive in my decisions and stayed within my comfort zone.
            </Card>
            <Card author="Amelia">
                I had the chance to have a styling session with Anikó. This is made up of 2 sessions, the first one was introductory where she explained
                the process, measured my body shape and understood more my profile and preferences via a test.<br/><br/>

                The second session was a wardrobe restyling. I had the opportunity to tell her which were the clothes that I struggled to wear and did not
                make me feel comfortable. She used her time and expertise to match them with new other pieces of clothing that could be suitable and let me
                try different options.<br/><br/>

                The outcome was unexpected and she succeeded in combining the right colours of clothings with my body shape in order to give value to my
                figure and make me feel more attractive and confident. She also created a digital portfolio with my clothes, my pictures and the different
                combinations of clothes for me to check every time I need.<br/><br/>

                Since this meeting, I started following her suggestions and changed my dressing approach at work and in social life. My husband and many
                friends and colleagues were very appreciative of my renewed appearance and each compliment made my day.<br/><br/>

                Thanks Aniko, your counselling was professional and respectful and made me feel at ease giving me a boost of confidence for my professional
                and personal life. This is something that every woman should do.
            </Card>
            <Card author="Irina">
                I had a chance to do a colour analysis with Aniko, and it was a very interesting experience for me, as I thought I knew my style and my colours…<br/>
                But there was some surprise for myself. She showed me how some colours really can be suitable for my skin tone, and some are against my skin.
                I will definitely use new skills in my next shopping trip.
            </Card>
            <Card author="Debbie">
                It was an amazing experience. After reviewing my wardrobe she found 10 different and exciting new outfits for me to wear out of my existing
                collection too which I hadn’t considered before. She carefully colour matched the outfits and accessorised them with jewellery and scarves to
                create a new me! I really enjoyed the whole experience and would recommend it to anyone!
            </Card>
        </div>
    </NormalBlock>
</Base>
